{
 "encounter_id": "00708",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good morning. I'll be precise: I started rosuvastatin eight weeks ago, and I have joint aches since, in my hands and knees."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, that helps. Tell me about the aches, which joints, when?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Both hands, particularly the knuckles, and both knees. Worse in the morning, easing by about ten."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any swelling or redness in the joints?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No visible swelling. No redness."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what are you taking?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Rosuvastatin, 10 mg once a day, in the evening. Nothing else at all."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What conditions do you have?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "High cholesterol, which is why I started it, and osteoarthritis in the right hip, diagnosed last year."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you exercise?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I swim three times a week, one kilometre. I've done it for years."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any breathlessness, chest tightness, or cough, while we're checking you over?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing like that. My breathing's fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me take your numbers. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Please. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 66, blood pressure 120 over 74, temperature 36.5, oxygen 99 percent, weight 71 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All as I'd expect. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Now, when you say it began after the statin, can you narrow it down? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Around week three. But I'd had a cold in week two, so I can't be certain it's the tablet. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A sensible point. Joint aches are less typical than muscle aches with statins, but they do happen. I'd say a statin side effect is possible, rather than certain."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What else could it be? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Early inflammatory arthritis is on the list because of the morning stiffness in your knuckles, though the stiffness is brief. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Should I stop the rosuvastatin? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not yet. I'd like to arrange blood tests, to check your muscle enzymes, thyroid and inflammation markers, and an X-ray of both hands."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "When can I have them? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "This week. The nurse will take the bloods, and the X-ray department will book you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Excellent. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take paracetamol if the aches get in the way, but not more than the packet says."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I rarely take any. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you in two weeks with the results."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two weeks. I'll bring my notes. ~"
  }
 ],
